{"version":"ai-mcq-bank-v2-la-batch15-high-quality-rewritten-affected-2026-05-22-stem-fixed-inequality-rendering-fixed-student-facing-qc-2026-05-31-pt-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch2-foundations-counting-2026-06-11-pt-batch3-counting-probability-rules-2026-06-11-pt-batch4-conditioning-2026-06-11-pt-batch5-random-variables-2026-06-11-pt-batch6-discrete-distributions-2026-06-11-pt-batch7-distribution-foundations-2026-06-11-pt-batch8-continuous-expectation-2026-06-11-pt-batch9-non-week7-expectation-transform-2026-06-11-pt-batch10-non-week7-process-summary-2026-06-11-pt-batch11-non-week7-final-summary-shape-2026-06-11-quality-round1-2026-06-14-quality-round2-2026-06-14-quality-round3-2026-06-14-quality-round4-deep-2026-06-14+quality-round5-difficulty-2026-06-14+quality-round6-expression-2026-06-14+quality-round7-answer-cue-2026-06-14+quality-round8-answer-shape-2026-06-14+quality-round9-answer-position-2026-06-14+quality-round10-template-padding-2026-06-14+quality-round11-generic-stems-2026-06-14+quality-round12-deterministic-cleanup-2026-06-15+quality-pilot-deep-rework-2026-06-15","concept_id":"Year-1/2a-Math-III-Analysis/uniform-norm.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/2a-Math-III-Analysis/uniform-norm.html","questions":[{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is the uniform norm of a bounded function $f\\colon X\\to\\mathbb{R}$ defined?","options":["$\\|f\\|_\\infty = \\sup_{x\\in X}|f(x)|$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty = \\inf_{x\\in X}|f(x)|$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty = \\sum_{x\\in X}|f(x)|$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty = |f(0)|$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f33d071c7072f2579dd08ac1"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which prerequisite idea is directly used for $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["Differentiability","Compactness","Countability","Supremum"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"355f8616ae2740a289aa3dc8"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $g\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ defined by $g(x) = \\sin x$, what is $\\|g\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$1$","$0$","$\\pi$","$+\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2fe4af748effdf9f05fa5256"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f\\colon(0,+\\infty)\\to\\mathbb{R}$ defined by $f(x) = \\mathrm{e}^{-x}$, what is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$0$","$1$","$\\mathrm{e}$","$+\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1bc22f0a58a83d3334cbd3e8"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement connects the uniform norm with uniform convergence?","options":["$f_n\\rightrightarrows f$ on $X$ if and only if $\\|f_n\\|_\\infty = \\|f\\|_\\infty$ for every $n$.","$f_n\\rightrightarrows f$ on $X$ if and only if $f_n(x) = f(x)$ for one point $x$.","$f_n\\rightrightarrows f$ on $X$ if and only if $\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty$ is non-zero.","$f_n\\rightrightarrows f$ on $X$ if and only if $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty = 0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e46e341cd7c76f6964443483"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does the uniform norm measure?","options":["The average value of the function over its domain.","The derivative of the function at the largest point, no matter which values are selected.","The largest possible absolute size of the function over its domain, in the supremum sense.","The number of points in the domain."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4c9002ad971704a8b3448eeb"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x) = 5$ on a non-empty domain $X$. What is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$5$","$0$","$25$","It depends on the number of points in $X$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cc1e17e8b18b8e050b272143"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x) = x$ on $[0,2]$. What is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$1$","$0$","$2$","$\\frac{1}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"86b088a8ec5dd0336faf583e"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$ for bounded functions defined this way?","options":["Because the supremum of $|f(x)|$ is then finite.","Because only bounded functions are continuous.","Because unbounded functions have no values.","Because the maximum of $|f(x)|$ is always attained."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2f59d36c0f8a33dff2ed9dce"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which interpretation is incorrect for $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["It uses absolute values.","It uses a supremum over $X$.","It controls the whole domain at once.","It measures average error over the domain."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b19b0578283afc275ae099f1"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"If $\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty \\lt \\varepsilon$, what follows for each $x\\in X$?","options":["$|f_n(x)-f(x)| \\gt \\varepsilon$","$|f_n(x)-f(x)| \\lt \\varepsilon$","$f_n(x) = f(x)$ exactly.","$\\|f_n\\|_\\infty = \\varepsilon$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ab64806cc83e13c0363d38c8"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty = \\frac{1}{n}$. What follows?","options":["$f_n$ does not converge uniformly to $f$.","$f_n = f$ for every $n$.","$f_n\\rightrightarrows f$ on $X$.","$f$ is unbounded."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c314eaa30f6d7006bbec07a2"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is the uniform norm of a bounded function $f:X\\to\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$\\|f\\|_\\infty=\\inf_{x\\in X}|f(x)|$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty=\\sup_{x\\in X}|f(x)|$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty=f(0)$","$\\|f\\|_\\infty=\\sum_{x\\in X}f(x)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"38b0c122b52634a94b521cec"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is boundedness relevant for the uniform norm?","options":["It ensures the supremum of $|f|$ is finite.","It makes the function constant.","It makes the domain finite.","It removes absolute values from the formula."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a76e639eec27415a202ce87f"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does $\\|f\\|_\\infty$ measure?","options":["The largest size of $f$ over its whole domain, in the supremum sense","The value of $f$ at exactly one point, under all circumstances whatsoever.","The derivative of $f$.","The number of zeros of $f$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"aacc2ca94fb09d1b61785999"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_016","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x)=2$ on $X$, what is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$0$","$1$","$4$","$2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bec5930ce5e5b900d5f7c30c"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x)=x$ on $[-1,1]$, what is $\\|f\\|_\\infty$?","options":["$1$","$0$","$-1$","$2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ace6e31932e2efa71d5e94b6"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which function has uniform norm $1$ on $\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["$g(x)=x$","$g(x)=2x$","$g(x)=x^2$","$g(x)=\\sin x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5b79cefba2b8ffc9f829cad"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_019","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How does the uniform norm characterise uniform convergence?","options":["$f_n\\to f$ uniformly iff $\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty\\to0$.","$f_n\\to f$ uniformly iff $\\|f_n\\|_\\infty\\to\\infty$.","Uniform convergence does not use function differences.","Uniform convergence requires $\\|f\\|_\\infty=0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"19721b699948226f9d688d0e"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_uniform_norm_699a0953_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $\\|f_n-f\\|_\\infty \\lt 0.01$, what does this say about every $x\\in X$?","options":["$|f_n(x)-f(x)| \\lt 0.01$","$|f_n(x)-f(x)| \\gt 0.01$","$f_n(x)=f(x)$ exactly","$f_n$ is unbounded"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4a903de50a3d8c91559efaf0"}]}}